- When you create a new directory for a new LangGraph agent, check the error using "langgraph dev" command.
- If possible, call an interrupt function in the start of node function. (https://langchain-ai.github.io/langgraph/concepts/human_in_the_loop/#common-pitfalls)
- Should add description field to the interrupt function for frontend to display.

# Interrupt
In order to use the Inbox, you'll need to use this interrupt input & output schemas for both Python.

class HumanInterruptConfig(TypedDict):
    allow_ignore: bool
    allow_respond: bool
    allow_edit: bool
    allow_accept: bool


class ActionRequest(TypedDict):
    action: str
    args: dict

class HumanInterrupt(TypedDict):
    action_request: ActionRequest
    config: HumanInterruptConfig
    description: Optional[str]


class HumanResponse(TypedDict):
    type: Literal['accept', 'ignore', 'response', 'edit']
    args: Union[None, str, ActionRequest]


